# REVENANT — .gitignore
#
# IMPORTANT — DO NOT IGNORE .kiro/
# The Kiroween 2026 rules require the /.kiro directory (specs, hooks,
# steering) to be present at the root of the public repo. Adding it to
# .gitignore could disqualify the submission. The safeguard line below
# (`!.kiro/`) is a reminder only — git cannot un-ignore files inside an
# ignored directory — so the real protection is: never add a `.kiro`
# pattern anywhere in this file.
# Safeguard note (not an active ignore rule):
#   !.kiro/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*

# Local tooling (none yet — the app itself has no build step)
node_modules/

# Local scratch / secrets — never commit these
.env
.env.*
*.log
